  ],
  "steps": [
    "Preheat the oven to 400°F (200°C) and line a large rimmed baking sheet with parchment paper.",
    "Place the chicken breasts on one side of the prepared baking sheet. Rub them with 1 tablespoon of olive oil, minced garlic, dried oregano, half of the salt, and half of the black pepper.",
    "Arrange the trimmed asparagus on the empty side of the baking sheet. Drizzle the asparagus with the remaining 1 tablespoon of olive oil, fresh lemon juice, and the remaining salt and pepper, tossing to coat. Place thin lemon slices over the chicken and asparagus.",
    "Bake in the preheated oven at 400°F (200°C) for 15 to 18 minutes, until the chicken reaches an internal temperature of 165°F (74°C) on a digital meat thermometer and the asparagus is tender-crisp.",
    "Remove from the oven, let the chicken rest for 5 minutes, then serve warm."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Ensure chicken breasts are pounded to an even thickness so they cook at the same rate as the asparagus.",
    "Store leftovers in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days."
  ],
  "storage": "Keeps well in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.",
